{"id":461,"name":"weavile","speciesId":461,"dex":461,"form":"normal","generation":4,"types":["dark","ice"],"stats":{"hp":70,"attack":120,"defense":65,"special-attack":45,"special-defense":85,"speed":125},"abilities":[{"name":"pressure","hidden":false},{"name":"pickpocket","hidden":true}],"height":11,"weight":340,"baseExp":179,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/461.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/461.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/461.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/461.ogg","genus":"Sharp Claw Pokémon","flavor":[{"version":"diamond","text":"They live in cold regions, forming groups of four or five that hunt prey with impressive coordination."},{"version":"pearl","text":"It sends signals to others by carving odd patterns in frost- covered trees and ice."},{"version":"platinum","text":"Evolution made it even more devious. It communicates by clawing signs in boulders."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It lives in snowy regions. It carves patterns in trees with its claws as a signal to others."},{"version":"black-2","text":"They communicate by clawing signs in boulders and work together to surround enemies."},{"version":"sun","text":"They travel in groups of four or five, leaving signs for one another on trees and rocks. They bring down their prey with coordinated attacks."},{"version":"moon","text":"They dwell in cold places. This Pokémon’s main food source in Alola is Vulpix and Sandshrew, which they carefully divide among their group."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"One Weavile will trip a Sandshrew and flip it over, and then another Weavile will deal the finishing blow with its sharp claws."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Thanks to its increased intelligence, scrapping over food is a thing of 